:"2026-11-11T11:13:34.388167Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.38853Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.454546Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.388499Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.45366Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":4,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"           train_missing  train_%  test_missing\nairline             4613    11.53         548.0\ndays_left           4438    11.10         696.0\ndeparture           4792    11.98         920.0\nduration            3013     7.53         582.0\nstops               2319     5.80         651.0","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>train_missing</th>\n      <th>train_%</th>\n      <th>test_missing</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>airline</th>\n      <td>4613</td>\n      <td>11.53</td>\n      <td>548.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>days_left</th>\n      <td>4438</td>\n      <td>11.10</td>\n      <td>696.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>departure</th>\n      <td>4792</td>\n      <td>11.98</td>\n      <td>920.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>duration</th>\n      <td>3013</td>\n      <td>7.53</td>\n      <td>582.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>stops</th>\n      <td>2319</td>\n      <td>5.80</td>\n      <td>651.0</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"82ff65b8-c800-4a2d-b3c2-3c4bc0c53fb4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"`airline`, `departure`, `stops`, `duration`, `days_left` have roughly 6–12 % missing values; the target has none. Dropping rows would throw away a large share of the data, so we impute.\n\n**Smart imputation using the `flight` code** (a flight code always maps to one airline, and the same flight on the same route almost always has the same departure slot, stops and duration):\n* `airline` ← airline seen with the same flight code (some codes were mangled to `0.00E+00`-style strings by Excel – they are all IndiGo `6E-…`, and still resolve consistently via the flight code).\n* `departure`, `stops` ← most frequent value for the same flight + source + destination.\n* `duration` ← median for the same flight + source + destination.\n* `days_left` is a booking-time attribute that the flight code cannot reveal, so it (and any leftovers) → `SimpleImputer` inside the model pipeline (mode for categoricals, median for numbers), fitted only on training folds so there is no leakage.\n\nOnly features (never the target) are used for this lookup, and test rows are used only to complete the lookup table, which is legitimate because no labels are involved.","metadata":{}},{"id":"4e0322b6-6172-4bdf-be8a-4168bce052c0","cell_type":"code","source":"full = pd.concat([train.assign(_set=\"train\"), test.assign(_set=\"test\")], ignore_index=True)\n\n# airline via flight code\nf2a = full.dropna(subset=[\"airline\"]).groupby(\"flight\").airline.agg(lambda s: s.mode().iat[0])\nfull[\"airline\"] = full[\"airline\"].fillna(full[\"flight\"].map(f2a))\n# departure / stops / duration via flight+route\nkey = [\"flight\", \"source\", \"destination\"]\nfor c in [\"departure\", \"stops\"]:\n    m = full.dropna(subset=[c]).groupby(key)[c].agg(lambda s: s.mode().iat[0]).rename(\"_m\")\n    full[c] = full[c].fillna(full.join(m, on=key)[\"_m\"])\nm = full.dropna(subset=[\"duration\"]).groupby(key)[\"duration\"].median().rename(\"_m\")\nfull[\"duration\"] = full[\"duration\"].fillna(full.join(m, on=key)[\"_m\"])\nprint(\"Missing after flight-based imputation:\\n\", full.drop(columns=\"price\").isna().sum()[lambda s: s > 0])","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.456972Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.457218Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.407215Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:34.457198Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.406395Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Missing after flight-based imputation:\n airline         7\ndeparture      35\nstops          13\nduration       30\ndays_left    5134\ndtype: int64\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"id":"156cd08d-5f11-41a4-ab83-ffd232c1be63","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Duplicates","metadata":{}},{"id":"c228ad27-c0cd-4221-a31b-70f00fcff6cd","cell_type":"code","source":"feat_cols = [c for c in train.columns if c != \"id\"]\nprint(\"Duplicate rows in train (ignoring id):\", train.duplicated(subset=feat_cols).sum())\nprint(\"Duplicate ids:\", train.id.duplicated().sum())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.408409Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.408807Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.447498Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.408776Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.446697Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Duplicate rows in train (ignoring id): 250\nDuplicate ids: 0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"79a4c985-7fd6-4fa5-8277-5fb749637c73","cell_type":"markdown","source":"Exact duplicates (all features **and** price) add no information and would leak between train/validation splits, so we drop them from the training set (test rows are never dropped).","metadata":{}},{"id":"1964d85f-1c89-4914-9554-2e0027f700b7","cell_type":"code","source":"full_train = full[full._set == \"train\"].drop(columns=\"_set\")\ndup_mask = train.duplicated(subset=feat_cols).values   # computed on raw data, same row order\nfull_train = full_train[~dup_mask].reset_index(drop=True)\nfull_test = full[full._set == \"test\"].drop(columns=[\"_set\", \"price\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\nprint(\"Train after de-duplication:\", full_train.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.44858Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.449498Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.529708Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.44947Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.528811Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Train after de-duplication: (39750, 12)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"f228d518-d740-445b-a246-15459de77847","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Outliers","metadata":{}},{"id":"9254d9ae-00ca-4476-a85e-dac80d45125a","cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\nfor a, c in zip(ax, [\"price\", \"duration\", \"days_left\"]):\n    sns.boxplot(x=full_train[c], ax=a, color=\"#4c78a8\"); a.set_title(f\"Boxplot of {c}\")\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\ndef iqr_outliers(s):\n    q1, q3 = s.quantile([.25, .75]); i = q3 - q1\n    return ((s < q1 - 1.5*i) | (s > q3 + 1.5*i)).sum()\nprint({c: int(iqr_outliers(full_train[c].dropna())) for c in [\"price\", \"duration\", \"days_left\"]})\nprint(\"Outlier price share inside each class (IQR rule within class):\")\nfor cl, g in full_train.groupby(\"class\"): print(cl, int(iqr_outliers(g.price)), \"of\", len(g))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.530701Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.530957Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:36.108931Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:35.530935Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:36.108159Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1500x400 with 3 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"{'price': 14, 'duration': 244, 'days_left': 0}\nOutlier price share inside each class (IQR rule within class):\nBusiness 515 of 12331\nEconomy 1929 of 27419\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":8},{"id":"e46a63dc-0c46-4ea5-9a4a-28309fdf9836","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Decision: retain the outliers.**\n* Prices are bimodal because Business tickets cost ~8× Economy. Judged globally, many Business fares look like outliers, but *within* each class only a small share is extreme.\n* The high prices are genuine (long multi-stop itineraries, last-minute bookings), the test set will contain the same kind of rows, and removing them would make the model under-predict exactly those cases.\n* Long durations (up to ~47 h) correspond to multi-stop itineraries and are real, not errors; no non-positive durations or negative days exist.\n* To limit the influence of the right-skewed price on the models, we train on `log1p(price)` instead of deleting rows.","metadata":{}},{"id":"c8488317-9cf7-4e58-b46a-c4bfd4331c90","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. Visualisations and insights","metadata":{}},{"id":"5c2e2548-59b4-4fef-855d-6d78ac23774e","cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\nsns.histplot(full_train.price, bins=60, kde=True, ax=ax[0], color=\"#4c78a8\"); ax[0].set_title(\"Price distribution\")\nsns.histplot(np.log1p(full_train.price), bins=60, kde=True, ax=ax[1], color=\"#f58518\"); ax[1].set_title(\"log1p(price) distribution\")\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:36.109988Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:36.11027Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.122552Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:36.110247Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.121546Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1300x400 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":9},{"id":"aca4fbe3-538a-4d26-a85c-c533f632dd99","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insight 1:** price is right-skewed and bimodal (Economy vs Business). The log transform makes it far more symmetric, which suits regression models.","metadata":{}},{"id":"0f23138e-d8f7-44f3-a481-5a2178e4e3b5","cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4.5))\nsns.boxplot(data=full_train, x=\"class\", y=\"price\", ax=ax[0]); ax[0].set_title(\"Price by class\")\norder = full_train.groupby(\"airline\").price.median().sort_values().index\nsns.boxplot(data=full_train, x=\"airline\", y=\"price\", order=order, ax=ax[1]); ax[1].set_title(\"Price by airline\"); ax[1].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=30)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.123948Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.124784Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.592546Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.124759Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.591623Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1400x450 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":10},{"id":"7a75016c-ecb1-4b0c-99ce-7f54ea407179","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insight 2:** class is the dominant driver – Business median is roughly 8–9× Economy. Only Vistara (~48 % Business) and Air India (~42 %) sell Business seats, so they look pricier than the budget carriers mostly because of this class mix.","metadata":{}},{"id":"dc73860a-5771-440d-881b-36d97e3c96c1","cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4.5))\nsns.lineplot(data=full_train, x=\"days_left\", y=\"price\", hue=\"class\", errorbar=None, ax=ax[0]); ax[0].set_title(\"Mean price vs days left before departure\")\nsns.boxplot(data=full_train, x=\"stops\", y=\"price\", order=[\"zero\", \"one\", \"two_or_more\"], ax=ax[1]); ax[1].set_title(\"Price by number of stops\")\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.593606Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.593896Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.098937Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:37.593863Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.098034Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1400x450 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":11},{"id":"01808eab-6f37-453f-88e9-1c959aa58894","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insight 3:** Economy fares jump when the departure is close (mean ≈ ₹11k within 7 days vs ≈ ₹5k when booked 30+ days ahead); Business fares move much less. Non-stop flights are clearly cheapest; one stop and two-or-more stops have similar medians.","metadata":{}},{"id":"00df9f06-fe92-4e60-aed3-cfd9f72b7278","cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4.5))\nsns.scatterplot(data=full_train.sample(5000, random_state=RS), x=\"duration\", y=\"price\", hue=\"class\", alpha=.5, ax=ax[0]); ax[0].set_title(\"Price vs duration\")\ncorr = full_train[[\"duration\", \"days_left\", \"price\"]].corr()\nsns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap=\"coolwarm\", vmin=-1, vmax=1, ax=ax[1]); ax[1].set_title(\"Correlation (numerical)\")\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.099955Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.100196Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.779734Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.100176Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.778808Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1400x450 with 3 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"8547a813-e99b-44dc-8789-62c6060ac1a1","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insight 4:** duration has a modest positive correlation with price (≈0.2) and days_left a weak negative one (≈-0.1). Linear correlations are weak because class shifts the price level, and the days_left effect is strongest only for Economy – which motivates non-linear/tree models and interactions.","metadata":{}},{"id":"0e15cbb6-b29c-4deb-96eb-cb7716901d3f","cell_type":"code","source":"pivot = full_train.pivot_table(index=\"source\", columns=\"destination\", values=\"price\", aggfunc=\"mean\")\nplt.figure(figsize=(7, 5)); sns.heatmap(pivot, annot=True, fmt=\".0f\", cmap=\"YlOrRd\"); plt.title(\"Mean price by route\"); plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.780786Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.781077Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.054492Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:38.781046Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.053614Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 700x500 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":13},{"id":"9afdcd90-ccd2-414f-9441-3b874367605c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insight 5:** mean price by route ranges from about ₹17k to ₹26k – a moderate effect, much smaller than class, and partly reflecting the class mix on each route.","metadata":{}},{"id":"48464403-a303-47cc-ac80-c851844437a9","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Feature engineering, encoding and scaling\n* **Engineered feature:** `route` (source_destination). Interactions such as class × duration are left to the models.\n* `flight` (869 unique codes, one-to-one with airline) is dropped – too high-cardinality and mostly redundant with airline/route; `id` is dropped.\n* **Encoding:** `stops` and `class` are naturally ordered → ordinal encoding (zero<one<two_or_more; Economy<Business). Nominal columns (airline, source, destination, departure, arrival, route) → one-hot encoding, so no fake order is introduced.\n* **Scaling:** `duration` and `days_left` are standardised (StandardScaler) for distance/gradient/regularisation-based models (Linear, Ridge, Lasso, KNN). Tree-based models are invariant to scaling, but we use the same pipeline for all models for a fair comparison – it doesn't hurt them.\n* **Target:** `log1p(price)` for training; predictions are transformed back with `expm1` and every metric below is reported in the **original rupee scale**.","metadata":{}},{"id":"2a519747-1f63-43db-aa35-96f3fa0fa9fb","cell_type":"code","source":"def add_features(d):\n    d = d.copy()\n    d[\"route\"] = d[\"source\"] + \"_\" + d[\"destination\"]\n    return d\nXall = add_features(full_train.drop(columns=[\"id\", \"flight\", \"price\"]))\ny = np.log1p(full_train[\"price\"].values)\nX_test = add_features(full_test.drop(columns=[\"id\", \"flight\"]))\n\nnum_f = [\"duration\", \"days_left\"]\nord_f = [\"stops\", \"class\"]\nnom_f = [\"airline\", \"source\", \"destination\", \"departure\", \"arrival\", \"route\"]\ndef make_pre():\n    return ColumnTransformer([\n        (\"num\", Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")), (\"sc\", StandardScaler())]), num_f),\n        (\"ord\", Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n                          (\"enc\", OrdinalEncoder(categories=[[\"zero\", \"one\", \"two_or_more\"], [\"Economy\", \"Business\"]]))]), ord_f),\n        (\"nom\", Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n                          (\"enc\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=False))]), nom_f),\n    ])\ndef pipe(model): return Pipeline([(\"pre\", make_pre()), (\"m\", model)])\n\nX_tr, X_val, y_tr, y_val = train_test_split(Xall, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=RS)\nprint(X_tr.shape, X_val.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.057431Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.057731Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.102168Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.057706Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.10137Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"(31800, 10) (7950, 10)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":14},{"id":"a3cb018c-7f8b-4890-b98a-9c8cdbb33027","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Model building (9 different models)\nMetrics on the 20 % validation set, in rupees.","metadata":{}},{"id":"1a2fef10-9196-421c-b187-22755e0c4e29","cell_type":"code","source":"def evaluate(p, name):\n    pred = np.expm1(p.predict(X_val)); true = np.expm1(y_val)\n    return {\"Model\": name, \"RMSE\": np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(true, pred)), \"MAE\": mean_absolute_error(true, pred), \"R2\": r2_score(true, pred)}\n\nbase_models = {\n    \"Linear Regression\": LinearRegression(),\n    \"Ridge\": Ridge(alpha=1.0),\n    \"Lasso\": Lasso(alpha=0.001),\n    \"KNN\": KNeighborsRegressor(n_neighbors=10),\n    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeRegressor(max_depth=12, random_state=RS),\n    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=150, n_jobs=-1, random_state=RS),\n    \"Extra Trees\": ExtraTreesRegressor(n_estimators=150, n_jobs=-1, random_state=RS),\n    \"Gradient Boosting\": GradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=RS),\n    \"HistGradientBoosting\": HistGradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=RS),\n}\nresults, fitted = [], {}\nfor n, m in base_models.items():\n    t = time.time(); p = pipe(m).fit(X_tr, y_tr); fitted[n] = p\n    r = evaluate(p, n); r[\"Time(s)\"] = round(time.time() - t, 1); results.append(r)\nbase_df = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values(\"RMSE\").reset_index(drop=True)\nbase_df","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.103202Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.103452Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T11:14:17.328155Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-11T11:13:39.103432Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T11:14:17.327479Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":15,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"                  Model          RMSE          MAE        R2  Time(s)\n0         Random Forest   3646.397631  1835.017479  0.974903     13.7\n1           Extra Trees   3761.088235  1799.096913  0.973299     14.2\n2  HistGradientBoosting   4691.385576  2625.870401  0.958456      1.4\n3         Decision Tree   4791.904322  2574.745459  0.956657      0.4\n4     Gradient Boosting   5331.246130